    what: "tests/e2e_gate_truth.rs (--features hook-tests) - the epic e2e, composing all four fixes at one seam over a hermetic temp repo through the real xtask binary, the real pre-merge-commit hook and real git. A WU adds a component, retires its design per DEC-16 and cites it at the bytes the build read (P1/DEC-28, judged at its last state per DEC-29); the mr commit that lands its report reports landing, not error: (P2a); the report is link-checked red then green (P2b); the merge is refused for a signer this checkout does not list, naming the signer and the roster, then accepted for a listed one (P3). Each WU deferred this step in identical words; it is paid here. Regression proof: against an xtask built at the epic base 1c8d587 it reds at exactly P1 (does not resolve at the tip), P3 (no valid mr/v1 note) and P2b (ungoverned, not checked). E-DFLOW s design-flow e2e (xtask/tests/e2e_design_flow.rs, --features design-e2e) additionally gained the retired-design citation case in W2."
